event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":81,"item_id":"rs_06787185e4135c9d016ac92e068aa48195b446779cebf8bef3","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering testing strategy**\n\nI'm thinking about how to conduct a test using ports in my server environment. I want to focus on using a free port to spawn processes without needing extensive logging. Keeping the test simple seems important, so I'd rather not alter unnecessary logs. It sounds like I'll need to set up a single asynchronous lifecycle timeout for the test node to ensure everything runs smoothly. Let's figure out the best approach!"}

